WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.830
Continuous monitoring is the ongoing process of maintaining awareness of security posture,

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.984
control effectiveness, system changes, vulnerabilities, threats, and risk.

00:00:07.984 --> 00:00:12.714
It is not the same as running one assessment before launch and

00:00:12.714 --> 00:00:15.080
then assuming the system remains safe.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.656
Modern systems change constantly.

00:00:16.656 --> 00:00:20.598
Assets appear, identities are added, configurations drift, vulnerabilities are disclosed,

00:00:20.598 --> 00:00:22.964
incidents occur, and business use evolves.

00:00:22.964 --> 00:00:26.117
Monitoring exists because security posture is not static.

00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:31.636
A useful continuous monitoring program watches the parts of the environment that influence risk:

00:00:31.636 --> 00:00:34.395
assets, identities, configurations, logs, vulnerabilities, incidents, changes,

00:00:34.395 --> 00:00:35.578
and control evidence.

00:00:35.578 --> 00:00:39.126
It connects technical signals to operational and risk decisions.

00:00:39.126 --> 00:00:42.673
That means monitoring should not stop at displaying dashboards.

00:00:42.673 --> 00:00:47.798
It should help people understand what changed, why it matters, who owns it,

00:00:47.798 --> 00:00:50.163
and what action should happen next.

00:00:50.163 --> 00:00:56.076
The word continuous does not mean every signal is reviewed every second by a person.

00:00:56.076 --> 00:01:00.807
It means monitoring is built into normal operations and repeated at a

00:01:00.807 --> 00:01:02.778
cadence that fits the risk.

00:01:02.778 --> 00:01:05.143
Some signals may need near-real-time alerting.

00:01:05.143 --> 00:01:09.085
Others may support periodic review, trend analysis, or audit readiness.

00:01:09.085 --> 00:01:13.027
The right rhythm depends on criticality, exposure, sensitivity, regulatory context,

00:01:13.027 --> 00:01:15.392
and how quickly risk can change.

00:01:15.392 --> 00:01:17.363
Continuous monitoring is decision support.

00:01:17.363 --> 00:01:21.305
A dashboard that no one uses is not a program.

00:01:21.305 --> 00:01:24.853
A scan result with no owner is not remediation.

00:01:24.853 --> 00:01:29.583
A log stream with no retention or review plan is not evidence.

00:01:29.583 --> 00:01:33.525
Effective monitoring connects data to triage, escalation, remediation, risk acceptance,

00:01:33.525 --> 00:01:34.708
reporting, and improvement.

00:01:34.708 --> 00:01:38.255
The purpose is not to collect the most data;

00:01:38.255 --> 00:01:43.380
it is to make better security and risk decisions faster and more consistently.
